Package: iivDecomp
Type: Package
Title: Decompose Intraindividual Variability into Signal and Noise Components
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: person("Dahai", "Shui", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "user@example.com")
Description: Provides tools for decomposing observed intraindividual
    variability (IIV) in intensive longitudinal data into four components:
    true construct-related variability, measurement error, careless responding
    (insufficient effort responding; IER), and context effects. Implements an
    expectation-maximization (EM) mixture model, binary IER screening methods,
    and simulation utilities. Based on the framework described in "Disentangling
    Meaningful Intraindividual Variability From Careless Responding and
    Measurement Error" (manuscript under review).
